Article 1 Where a motor vehicle causes damage in a traffic accident, and the owner or manager of the motor vehicle falls under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court shall determine that it is at fault for the occurrence of the damage and apply the provisions of Article 1209 of the Civil Code to determine its corresponding compensation liability:
(1) It knew or should have known that the motor vehicle had defects, and such defects are one of the causes of the traffic accident;
(2) It knew or should have known that the driver did not hold a driving qualification or had not obtained the corresponding driving qualification;
(3) It knew or should have known that the driver, due to drinking alcohol, taking psychotropic drugs or narcotic drugs controlled by the State, or suffering from a disease that impedes safe driving of a motor vehicle, was legally unable to drive the motor vehicle; or
(4) Other circumstances under which the owner or manager of the motor vehicle shall be determined to be at fault.

Article 12 Where a road traffic accident causes the following property losses, and a party requests the tortfeasor to compensate, the People's Court shall support it:
(1) expenses incurred for repairing the damaged vehicle, losses of items carried in the vehicle, and vehicle rescue expenses;
(2) expenses for replacing the vehicle with a vehicle of equivalent value to the damaged vehicle at the time of the traffic accident due to the vehicle's destruction or irreparability;
(3) reasonable losses of a vehicle engaged in business activities such as cargo transportation or passenger transportation according to law due to its inability to engage in the corresponding business activities; and
(4) reasonable expenses for ordinary alternative means of transportation incurred by a non-business vehicle due to its inability to continue to be used.
III. Determination of Liability

Article 15 Where any of the following circumstances causes personal injury to a third party, and a party requests that the insurance company provide compensation within the limits of liability of the compulsory traffic accident liability insurance, the People's Court shall support it:
(1) The driver did not obtain a driving qualification or did not obtain the corresponding driving qualification;
(2) The driver drove a motor vehicle after drunk driving, taking psychotropic drugs or narcotic drugs controlled by the State, and caused a traffic accident;
(3) The driver intentionally caused a traffic accident.
Where the insurance company claims recourse against the tortfeasor within the scope of compensation, the People's Court shall support it. The limitation of action for the right of recourse shall be calculated from the date of the insurance company's actual compensation.
